Modifications by Rakazo contributors include, among others:
- Coding mode (OpenCode / Kilo on the bot's computer)
- Lightpanda page browser and the rakazo-captcha helper
- Periodic work-status messages
- Lite deployment profile for 8 GB machines (infra/compose/docker-compose.lite.yml)
- OpenAI-compatible provider presets and small-model mode
- Inline reasoning (<think>) stripping for local and open-weight models
- Self-improving learned skills after each run (packages/adapters/src/skill-learning.ts)
- Coding mode finish protocol (READY / EVIDENCE / BLOCKED) and stall detection
- Host free-memory gate for computers (infra/sandboxes/supervisor/src/memory-gate.ts)

Design credits (ideas, no code copied):
- The learned-skills loop follows the learning approach of Klex by stagewise
  (https://github.com/stagewise-io/klex), Apache License 2.0.
- The coding finish protocol, stall nudges and free-memory admission follow
  dori-superagent by Sisyphus Labs (https://github.com/sisyphuslabs/dori-superagent), MIT License.
